From 615d37e99bea4015e5179282e5797107bccdfaed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 15:48:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] build: drop the layers that cannot run on Android

After removing the Mono runtime and the desktop console drivers, four more
trees are left that this port never builds or ships:

- Runtimes/Unity/BepInEx.Unity.Mono still held two source files whose project
  file had just been deleted, so they compiled into nothing.
- Runtimes/Unity/Doorstop holds the Doorstop ini files and run_bepinex scripts
  used to launch a desktop game process. Nothing on Android uses Doorstop;
  AndroidEntrypoint is reached from libfusion instead.
- Runtimes/NET holds the .NET Framework/CoreCLR desktop hosts. These are not
  Unity runtimes and do not use the IL2CPP interop layer.
- build/ is the Cake packaging pipeline. Besides producing desktop
  distributions it downloads Doorstop, BepInEx/Dobby and a mini-coreclr zip
  from BepInEx release servers, which is a supply path this repository
  deliberately does not use: the runtime here is built from dotnet/runtime by
  its own workflow instead.

The solution keeps only the four projects the Android runtime needs, drops the
Release_NetFramework/Release_Unity configurations that existed for those
desktop distributions, and drops a SharedMSBuildProjectFiles section that
referenced a project file no longer present. Directory.Build.props is still
picked up automatically by MSBuild.

Depends-On: 0004-il2cpp-hook-through-libfusion-and-resolve-export-stu, 0006-core-delete-the-Mono-runtime
